All 15 tests now pass. Here are the fixes applied:

**`src/auth.py`**
- `has_permission`: compare lowercased role names so the check is case-insensitive.
- `is_admin_or_owner`: changed `and` to `or` so either being an admin *or* matching the owner grants access.

**`src/inventory.py`**
- `__init__`: removed the mutable default argument (`{}`) and instead initialize a fresh dict when no `initial` mapping is provided.
- `add`: accumulate stock with `+` instead of overwriting it.
- `reserve`: allow reserving exactly the available amount (`>` instead of `>=`).
- `release`: guard against over-releasing by raising `ValueError` when `qty > current`.

**`src/text_utils.py`**
- `slugify`: lowercased the input and used `re.sub` to collapse any run of non-alphanumeric characters into a single `-`, then stripped leading/trailing dashes.
- `truncate`: subtract the suffix length from the slice so the total output length never exceeds `max_len`.

No files under `tests/` were modified.
